B.R7=new A.fN("I had designed the onboarding from the inside out. I knew what the data was for \u2014 so I wrote flows that reflected that knowledge. But users arrive from the outside in. No context, no trust, no reason to believe that sharing their information produces anything worth the risk. I had built a consent model for the developer, not the user.",null,null,B.bl,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.R8=new A.fN("The data collection that makes matching useful is exactly what triggers trust concerns during onboarding. Asking for location or contacts upfront is experientially alarming \u2014 especially when the user has not yet seen any value.",null,null,B.bl,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.Rb=new A.fN("The redesigned onboarding cleared App Store review without a single violation. Firebase Analytics showed onboarding consent drop-off decreased by ~68%. Users who saw sample matches before any permission request completed the flow at a significantly higher rate. The driver wasn't better copy. It was sequencing.",null,null,B.bl,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
